      "dom_id": "question-340828",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$$\n$\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})=$\n {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fourth definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})}}{1-{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}}}{1-{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{1}{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}}{1-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+\\frac{1}{4})}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}÷\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
