    {
      "dom_id": "question-96551",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$$\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w)?$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe definition of $\\operatorname{coth}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}+1}{{e}^{2x}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{e}^{-2x}}{1-{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{coth}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w) & =\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w}+1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2w}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{w}^{2}}+1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4{w}^{2}}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{w}^{2}+1}{4{w}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "problem_field_keys": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
