  "tutorials": [
    {
      "dom_id": "step-32684",
      "name": "Introduction",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/75a56c2d21e2f2cf83a6635933aa5b3b4f4683fedef5f51430d0b1b171d8726b.svg)\n\nWe can define the **reciprocal hyperbolic functions** similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions. \n\nThe **hyperbolic cosecant function** (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/c112c1732880af3a22ea3831581062f4b7d8a96ad3408e9a98af0387691e9af7.svg)\nThe graph of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/1de5a1885eb15a44f9de1b9d170b8906f684c1784f5f67de840cca1628f2ec91.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/cc0b2c19d1606c8a0a2c11411a0b0a4fbc09f264d9d28d0fcb2fb81f6c576a8a.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/ea88889bed67f76a0de3b6f4d3acd48051d741d4c51b8013b69fd6642e30eac1.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/56c0f97156e3980b9cf25c7204e993714a0879ba463132c958267e5927e71f4c.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/e8eea575c16295c549b3019751f3562aa98b9d6f3e15375c24837521528878ca.svg)\n\n- It has a vertical asymptote ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\n- It has a horizontal asymptote ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198821/assets/6c63827e94b6c11a9803605bd54156d90d3fcc6ff4639dd179a5fb024bcffaa1.svg)\n\n- It is an odd function.",
