        "html": "<div class=\"step\" contentid=\"5205\" id=\"step-32684\" stepid=\"32684\" steptype=\"tutorial\" style=\"display: block\">\n<div class=\"stepHeader\">\n<div class=\"stepName\">\n<a class=\"stepAnchor\" id=\"stepAnchor-32684\" name=\"step-1\">Introduction</a>\n</div>\n<div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"32684\">?</div>\n</div>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" display=\"true\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg focusable=\"false\" height=\"0.036ex\" role=\"img\" style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"0.036ex\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>We can define the <strong>reciprocal hyperbolic functions</strong> similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions. </p>\n<p>The <strong>hyperbolic cosecant function</strong> (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as \n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" display=\"true\" jax=\"SVG\"><svg focusable=\"false\" height=\"4.774ex\" role=\"img\" style=\"vertical-align: -1.738ex;\" viewbox=\"0 -1342 13104.9 2110\" width=\"29.649ex\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><path d=\"M370 305T349 305T313 320T297 358Q297 381 312 396Q317 401 317 402T307 404Q281 408 258 408Q209 408 178 376Q131 329 131 219Q131 137 162 90Q203 29 272 29Q313 29 338 55T374 117Q376 125 379 127T395 129H409Q415 123 415 120Q415 116 411 104T395 71T366 33T318 2T249 -11Q163 -11 99 53T34 214Q34 318 99 383T250 448T370 421T404 357Q404 334 387 320Z\" data-c=\"63\"></path><path d=\"M295 316Q295 356 268 385T190 414Q154 414 128 401Q98 382 98 349Q97 344 98 336T114 312T157 287Q175 282 201 278T245 269T277 256Q294 248 310 236T342 195T359 133Q359 71 321 31T198 -10H190Q138 -10 94 26L86 19L77 10Q71 4 65 -1L54 -11H46H42Q39 -11 33 -5V74V132Q33 153 35 157T45 16